const DD=`\n\n=== DEFENSE DISCIPLINE (Eric-ruled 2026-07-18; protocol_debate_engine DD-1..DD-3) ===\n\nDD-1. SCOPE VS AMMUNITION. The debate's scope is the question and its citation CHAIN; the verse is ammunition, not the battlefield. A challenger's point about an isolated term or verse is answered by re-seating that term in its chain — context, grammar floor, cross-reference — never by adjudicating the term in isolation. A term stripped of its chain proves nothing and concedes nothing.\n\nDD-2. NO IN-ROUND CONCESSION. No concession, re-grade, or framework adjustment is ever made on the opponent's clock. The only in-battle response to a correction — however textually accurate — is: "Noted. Not conceding here. Goes to review." All self-examination happens in cold review: full record, our ground, opponent not in the room. A defense that concedes in-round to a context-stripped term is a defense-discipline slip and must be flagged in review even when the verdict still lands HELD.\n\nDD-3. CHAIN-SCOPED FRAMING — Isaiah 28:10 as rule of engagement. Debate topics are framed at the chain level: the framework's case is its interlocking citations — precept upon precept, line upon line, here a little, there a little — and the challenger must break the CHAIN, not one link. Isaiah 28:10 is declared in the topic framing as the rule of engagement; it is never cited inside L3 as a witness for a conclusion — that is citing the method as evidence, and DG-29 cuts both ways.`;const sys=I.dsys+DD;const msgs=[{role:'user',content:($('D1 Build').first().json.opening_user||'DEBATE TOPIC: '+I.topic)},{role:'assistant',content:$('D1 Extract').first().json.raw},{role:'user',content:'THE CHALLENGER ANSWERED:\n\n'+$('C1 Extract').first().json.raw+'\n\nRound 2. Tag every layer.'}];
return [{json:{run_token:TOK,round:'D2',call:call(R.defender,sys,msgs)}}];
